  "narrative": "No claim is currently supported by the accumulated evidence as a clinically meaningful predictor or subgroup association in this dataset. The due validations show that the strongest candidate did not replicate. H34 tested outcome_006 with feature_002=1 versus 0 within feature_034=0 under the stronger-dependency hypothesis. Discovery R27 gave signed effect +0.0395, about 22.5% of the absolute outcome_006 mean and well above the 10% threshold of about 0.0175, but independent validation R39 gave only +0.0072, about 4.1%, with interval [-0.0696, +0.0839]. The validation point estimate is below the clinical threshold, includes the null, and is inconsistent with the discovery magnitude. I therefore do not accept H34. I keep it unresolved but closed because the wide intervals still cannot formally exclude a clinically meaningful positive effect, while concluding that this subgroup localization is not a useful lead. This also weakens, but does not by itself kill, H13, the population outcome_006/feature_002 claim. H13 remains active because it is the only direct claim with a discovery point estimate above the threshold: R2 is +0.0209, about 11.9%, interval [-0.0139, +0.0556]. The subgroup failure suggests caution, but a population-level association could still replicate even if the feature_034=0 localization failed. H7 outcome_002/feature_050 validation R13 gives signed effect +0.0044, about 1.7%, after discovery R7 +0.0151, about 5.8%; both intervals include the null, and the validation upper bound remains above threshold. I keep H7 unresolved but closed: there is no support for a clinically meaningful effect, but absolute exclusion is not possible. H15 outcome_009/feature_042 was previously rejected because the discovery estimate was near null/opposite and its upper bound was below threshold. New validation R40 is also near null, signed +0.0019, about 0.7%, but its wide independent interval upper bound +0.0290 slightly crosses the threshold of about 0.0256.